# Build context hygiene — every image builds from the REPO ROOT context
# (docker build -f apps/<app>/Dockerfile .), so keep the context lean.
#
# NOTE: unlike .gitignore, a bare pattern here matches ONLY at the context root — nested
# exclusions need the **/ prefix, hence the doubled entries.

# VCS / editor / agent state
.git
.idea
.claude
**/.DS_Store

# Python
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.venv
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/*.egg-info

# Node
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.vite
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Local dev processes and logs (make up / make down)
.run
logs
**/*.log

# Env files never bake into an image — configuration is injected at run time. (The nested
# variant matters: a stray apps/interface/.env would be auto-loaded by vite build and bake
# local VITE_* overrides into the published bundle.)
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Model weights live in caches outside the repo, never in an image.
**/*.gguf
**/*.safetensors
**/*.bin
**/*.mlx

# Internal docs, fixtures, and scratch notes — not needed by any image.
docs
session-fixtures
detail-test-fixtures
*.md
!README.md
